Next_state logic: case current_state, OFF: if(j) next_state=ON else next_state=OFF; ON: if(k) next_state=OFF else next_state=ON; endcase

Output: assign out = current_state[1]; // since ON is 2'b01, the MSB is 1 for ON, 0 for OFF.

In one-hot encoding, OFF=2'b00, ON=2'b01, so out = current_state[1] gives 0 for OFF, 1 for ON, which matches the Moore output.

